{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nImplement only the lifecycle/ownership shape approved by the runner research story. This is a behavior-preserving ownership refactor plus any fault-proven correctness fixes; it is not a line-count exercise.\n\n## Approach\n\n- Add the fault-matrix tests before movement.\n- Move cohesive call-graph clusters into the existing owner selected by the research, or introduce one adequately sized sibling only if no existing owner fits.\n- Preserve one provider-resource owner, fallback model close-before-provider close ordering, failure spend/step accounting, answer-model attribution, success logging before potentially-raising finalization, final usage/run-shape/spend updates, and provider provenance.\n- Replace string monkeypatch/re-export dependencies with narrow injection only where the same change migrates every consumer.\n- Record before/after method/module measurements as evidence, never as a gate.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Only the runner-cluster files named by the prerequisite's approved ownership map [rebar:patriotic-valued-hog].\n- Focused runner/provider/cache/fallback/telemetry tests in `tests/unit/` and `tests/interfaces/`.\n- No project-wide policy, config-schema, provider API, or workflow-engine change.\n\n## Testing\n\nStart with the prerequisite's full fault matrix. Exercise a normal structured call, text call, fallback success, provider/capability failure, external-call failure after usage, finalization failure, and telemetry failure. Compare result/provenance/accounting shapes before and after; run the default suite plus lint/typecheck/complexity/module-size gates.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every fault-matrix test fails against the deliberately broken ordering/cleanup variant it guards and passes on the implementation.\n- [ ] Provider clients and fallback-owned clients close exactly once in the established order on success and every injected failure path.\n- [ ] Failed calls retain failure spend and step-failure accounting; successful calls retain answer attribution, pre-finalization log semantics, final result shape, usage, and spend.\n- [ ] The implementation follows the research-approved owner map and deletes superseded orchestration; it does not duplicate `ProviderSession`, `ExitStack`, settings builders, telemetry helpers, or provider/capability selection.\n- [ ] Every moved string/monkeypatch consumer is migrated in the same change; no compatibility re-export is retained solely to hide a broken test seam.\n- [ ] No function-size ratchet, per-file headroom check, hook/plugin bus, mechanically split sub-100-LOC module, or padding is added.\n- [ ] Default suite, focused runner/provider/cache/fallback/telemetry tests, lint, typecheck, complexity, and module-size gates pass with no behavioral delta except separately fault-proven fixes."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788026786748057720,"uuid":"e3bba794-ab11-4202-abc8-4ad73d9678bf"}